o and just get one of that  group and then we've got a seven left  over now if there was a seven and a two  left over you'd multiply those together  and that'd be 14 underneath the radical  and again if we had another group of  let's say threes then we would multiply  two times three that be six on the  outside so you're trying to make groups  of three right okay let's do another  example let's see if we can cruise on  down to number 23 okay so this one's the  cube root of 144  okay so cube root 144 let's do the prime  factorization method so we know 144 is  12 times 12 okay from our multiplication  facts right so 12 is 4 times 3 12 is 3  times 4 and then these fours we can  break down into 2 times 2 but remember  we're taking the cube root so that means  we're looking for groups of three right  so let's see there is a group of three  okay so that becomes 2 but look what we  have left over we have left over a 2 a 3  and a 3 so we want to multiply those  together we don't have enough to make  another group of three of the same  numbers so these are like kind of the  leftover the remainder 3 times 3 is 9  times 2 is 18 the 18 stays underneath  that radical and you've got it okay so I  hope this video helps you to understand  how to work with square roots and cube  roots and simplifying them again if you  want to download the worksheet go ahead  and check that link out in the  description below and I've got an answer  key so you can check your work otherwise  I look forward to seeing the future  videos let me know in the comments below  what you thought of this particular  format if it was helpful of course I'm  going to continue to do the regular  whiteboard videos that I've been doing  but again my goal is to help you to  boost your score in your math class  improve your understanding and hopefully  make learning math a lot less stressful  and so that's what these videos are all  about so if that's helping you let me  know and I look forward to seeing you in  the future videos

